A macOS user installs a signed Subset Usage app, sees their lowest remaining AI subscription quota in the menu bar, and opens the full usage dashboard from it, without installing Node or running a terminal command.

## Context

The usage pilot (SET-1) runs today as the local `@sub-set/usage` CLI (`packages/usage-cli`: `subset-usage serve|status|collect`, loopback-only server, bundled `@subset/usage` runtime and `apps/usage` view). The tag-based npm publish workflow exists but nothing is published yet. Installed Claude/Antigravity status-line collectors call a stable shim at `~/.local/share/subset/bin/subset-usage-collect`, which `serve` rewrites to point at the current runtime.

## Completion gate

All children are done, and a signed, notarized build has been installed on a clean macOS account and shows live usage from at least ChatGPT and Claude. Only then may the catalog list a macOS surface (AGENTS.md: publish only working availability). This parent is a container, not an implementation slice.

## Exclusions

iOS, Windows, Linux tray builds; a hosted or synced version; any change to which local sign-ins are read (that list is governed by the AGENTS.md exception)."},
"shell": {"title": "Run the usage runtime inside a Tauri menu-bar shell", "description": "## Behavior

Launching the app starts the usage runtime on 127.0.0.1 with a free port, shows a menu-bar icon, and opens the existing dashboard in a popover or window when clicked. Quitting stops the runtime and frees the port. No Dock icon by default.

## Decision needed first

How the runtime ships: (a) bundle a Node 22 sidecar plus `dist/cli.mjs` and `web/` (fast, ~40-60 MB, keeps one codebase), (b) a Node single-executable app as the sidecar, or (c) port the server/readers to Rust. Recommendation: (a) or (b) now; revisit (c) only if size or startup is a problem.

## Scope

New `native/usage-menubar/` Tauri v2 target that embeds the built `@sub-set/usage` artifacts. The collector shim must point at the bundled runtime after first launch, and existing collectors must keep working (the CLI's migration already rewrites only exact recorded collector commands). The webview loads only the loopback dashboard; the API guard header (`X-Subset-Request`) and Host/Origin checks stay in force.

## Acceptance evidence

- Launch, open, close, and quit on macOS 15+ with no orphaned runtime process (checked with `lsof`/`ps`).
- Port collision falls back to a free port.
- An installed Claude collector keeps collecting after switching from the CLI to the app.
- Keychain prompts for local sign-ins name the app and "Always Allow" persists across relaunch; document the identity change from the CLI's `node` binary.

## Verification

Manual macOS run recorded in the PR, plus a scripted smoke test that starts the bundled sidecar and checks `/api/status` with the guard header."},
"tray": {"title": "Show usage status in the menu-bar icon and menu", "description": "## Behavior

The menu-bar item shows the lowest remaining percentage (or an alert glyph when a window is exhausted or an account needs attention). Its menu lists each account's provider, name or email, remaining percent, and next reset, plus Refresh, Open dashboard, Settings, and Quit. It refreshes on the dashboard's auto-refresh interval and pauses while the Mac sleeps.

## Scope

Reads the existing `status` contract (`@subset/usage` schema version 1) from the runtime; no new provider reads and no credentials in the menu. Respects the used/remaining display preference. Stale or failed reads show their observation time and error instead of old numbers presented as current.

## Acceptance evidence

- Exhausted, running-low, stale, and failed-read states each render distinctly (fixture-driven test).
- VoiceOver reads the menu items; keyboard navigation works.
- Light and dark menu bars render the template icon correctly.

## Dependencies

Blocked by the Tauri shell issue (needs the running runtime and port)."},
